\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The fibre of $F$ over $(-\tfrac  14,0,0)$ projected to the $(y,z)$ plane. The three points lie on the parabola $12y^2=4z+1$, which is the second element of the lex basis~\eqref  {eq:basis}, and satisfy $y(2z-13)=0$, that is $y=0$ or $z=\tfrac  {13}2$; the coordinate $x=-\tfrac  23y$ then follows from the first element.}}{29}{figure.88}\protected@file@percent }
